# Fix LESS syntax highlighting

## What this issue is about
This issue focuses on a bug in the LESS syntax highlighting when using `@import` statements within selectors. The highlighting fails in Pygments, causing some legitimate LESS code to be marked as invalid, even though it works in other environments like the Less Sandbox.

## What needs to be done
We need to improve the LESS syntax highlighting to account for these `@import` statements inside selectors. Some discussions indicate that the underlying issues may be linked to Pygments and have been reported there, but no fix has been implemented yet.

## Helpful background
The problematic code examples are as follows:
- 
```less
.loadThemeFonts() {
  @import "./typography.css";
}
```
- 
```less
.highlight {
  .highlight-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;

    h2 {
      text-align: center;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
  }
}
```
Although temporary workarounds exist (such as changing the lexer to `css` or `text`), these are not optimal.

## Good first steps
1. Review the existing code in `docs/source/theming/custom-styling.md` to understand how the current syntax highlighting is working.
2. Follow the ongoing discussions in the related Pygments issues ([#2606](https://github.com/pygments/pygments/issues/2606) and [#2817](https://github.com/pygments/pygments/issues/2817)).
3. Consider proposing improvements to the documentation to reflect these issues and possible workarounds.

Feel free to reach out if you have questions or need guidance!
